==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|nb|No-nor-falle (verb).ogg|Audio (Standard East Norwegian)}}

===Etymology 1===
Derived from the verb ''falle'', also influenced by [[German]].

====Noun====
{{nb-noun-m1}}

# a slanted metal piece in a door lock that moves when pressing the handle.

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|nb|non|falla}}, "to fall", from {{der|nb|gem-pro|*fallaną}}, from {{der|nb|ine-pro|*pōl-}}. Cognates include [[Faeroese]] and {{cog|sv|falla}}, {{cog|da|falde}}, {{cog|en|fall}}, {{cog|de|fallen}}.

====Verb====
{{head|nb|verb|present tense|faller|past tense|falt|past participle|falt|present participle|fallende|imperative|fall}}

# to [[fall]]
#: {{ux|nb|Han skled, mistet fotfestet og '''falt.'''|He slipped, lost his footing and '''fell'''.}}
#: {{ux|nb|Byen '''falt''' etter en måneds beleiring.|The city '''fell''' after being laid siege to for a month.}}
#: {{ux|nb|Prisene på klær '''falt''' dramatisk i fjor.|Prices on clothes '''fell''' dramatically last year.}}
# to [[fall]], [[die]]
#: {{ux|nb|Faren min '''falt''' i krigen.|My father '''died''' in the war.}}
#: {{ux|nb|Mange mennesker '''falt''' i slaget.|Many people '''fell''' in the battle.}}
# to [[slope]]
#: {{ux|nb|Det nye gulvet '''faller''' ganske mye.|The new floor '''slopes''' quite a bit.}}
# to look, fit [adjective/adverb] on
#: {{ux|nb|Skaftet på denne kniven '''faller''' godt i hånden.|The handle of this knife '''fits''' well in my hand.}}
#: {{ux|nb|Kjolen '''faller''' fint.|The dress '''looks''' nice.}}
# (''with adjectives'') to seem, appear
#: {{ux|nb|Det '''faller''' naturlig for henne.|It '''comes''' natural for her.}}
#: {{ux|nb|Det '''faller''' naturlig å gjøre det nå.|It '''seems''' only natural to do it now.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* (''to fall'') {{l|nb|dale}}, {{l|nb|deise}}, {{l|nb|dette}}, {{l|nb|dratte}}, {{l|nb|drysse}}, {{l|nb|dumpe}}, {{l|nb|gli}}, {{l|nb|gå}} {{l|nb|på}} {{l|nb|hodet}}, {{l|nb|gå}} {{l|nb|over}} {{l|nb|ende}}, {{l|nb|plumpe}}, {{l|nb|ramle}}, {{l|nb|rape}}, {{l|nb|rause}}, {{l|nb|segne}}, {{l|nb|seise}}, {{l|nb|snuble}}, {{l|nb|snåve}}, {{l|nb|strømme}} {{l|nb|ned}}, {{l|nb|stupe}}, {{l|nb|styrte}}, {{l|nb|tryne}}, {{l|nb|tumle}}, {{l|nb|velte}}
* (''to die, be slain'') {{l|nb|dø}}, {{l|nb|omkomme}}, {{l|nb|bukke}} ([[gå]]) {{l|nb|under}}
* (''to look, fit'') {{l|nb|føre}} {{l|nb|seg}}, {{l|nb|henge}}, {{l|nb|ligge}}, {{l|nb|ta}} {{l|nb|seg}} {{l|nb|ut}}, {{l|nb|være}}
* (''to decrease, fall'') {{l|nb|avta}}, {{l|nb|ebbe}} {{l|nb|ut}}, {{l|nb|legge}} {{l|nb|seg}}, {{l|nb|minke}}, {{l|nb|synke}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|nb|fall}} = a fall
* {{l|nb|falleferdig}} = [[tumbledown]], [[ramshackle]]
* {{l|nb|fallen}}
* '''falle''' bort = lapse, cease to apply, be discontinued (literally: "fall away")
* '''falle''' for noe/noen = fall for something/someone
* '''falle''' fra hverandre = fall to pieces (literally: "fall from each other")
* '''falle''' heldig ut = be a success, turn out well (literally: "fall out luckily")
* '''falle''' noen inn = occur to someone (literally: "fall someone in", "fall in to someone")
* '''falle''' pladask for noen = fall head over heels in love with someone (literally: "fall smack for someone")
* '''falle''' sammen = collapse, break down, tumble down, fall down (literally: "fall together")
* '''falle''' sammen med = be identical with, coincide with (literally: "fall together with")
* '''falle''' seg slik = it so happens (literally: "fall like this")
* '''falle''' så lang en er = fall full length (literally: "fall as long as one is")
* '''falle''' til ro = settle, settle down (literally: "fall to order")
* '''falle''' i hendene på noen = fall into the hands of somebody
* '''falle''' i ens smak = be to one's liking (literally: "fall in one's taste")
* {{l|nb|forfalle}}
* {{l|nb|overfalle}}
* ta noe som det '''faller''' seg = take something as it comes (literally: "take something as it falls")

